#: index.docbook:18
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "The smb ioslave enables you to browse the shares of a &Windows; (or Samba) network."
msgid "The smb worker enables you to browse the shares of a &Windows; (or Samba) network."
msgstr "O ioslave smb permítelle examinar as comparticións dunha rede &Windows; (ou Samba)."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 trunk5 stable6
#: index.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "To see the workgroups, enter <userinput><command>smb:/</command></userinput>."
msgstr "Para ver os grupos de traballo, insira <userinput><command>smb:/</command></userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 trunk5 stable6
#: index.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput><command>smb://</command><replaceable>a_workgroup</replaceable></userinput> will list the hosts in this workgroup."
msgstr "<userinput><command>smb://</command><replaceable>grupoTraballo</replaceable></userinput> enumerará os servidores dese grupo de traballo."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 trunk5 stable6
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "To see the shares of a host, enter <userinput><command>smb://</command><replaceable>the_host</replaceable></userinput> or <userinput><command>smb:/</command><replaceable>a_workgroup</replaceable>/<replaceable>the_host</replaceable></userinput>."
msgstr "Para ver as comparticións dun servidor, insira <userinput><command>smb://</command><replaceable>servidor</replaceable></userinput> ou <userinput><command>smb:/</command><replaceable>grupoTraballo</replaceable><replaceable>servidor</replaceable></userinput>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 trunk5 stable6
#: index.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "To access a share directly enter <userinput><command>smb://</command><replaceable>the_host/the_share</replaceable></userinput> or <userinput><command>smb:/</command><replaceable>a_workgroup</replaceable>/<replaceable>the_host</replaceable>/<replaceable>the_share</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr "Para acceder directamene a un servidor insira <userinput><command>smb://</command><replaceable>servidor/compartición</replaceable></userinput> ou <userinput><command>smb:/</command><replaceable>grupoTraballo</replaceable>/<replaceable>servidor</replaceable>/<replaceable>compartición</replaceable></userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 trunk5 stable6
#: index.docbook:44
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "The smb ioslave requires that you have libsmbclient to use this ioslave."
msgid "The smb worker requires that you have libsmbclient to use this worker."
msgstr "O ioslave smb require que teña instalada libsmbclient para usalo."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 trunk5 stable6
#: index.docbook:48
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "You can set your default user name and password in the &systemsettings; category <guilabel>Network and Connectivity</guilabel> in <menuchoice><guisubmenu>Sharing</guisubmenu><guimenuitem> Windows Shares</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This is especially useful if you are a member of a &Windows; <acronym>NT</acronym> domain. There you can also set your workgroup name, but in most cases this is not required. The kioslave will ask for your username and password if a default is not set."
msgid "You can set your default user name and password in the &systemsettings; category <guilabel>Network</guilabel> in <menuchoice><guisubmenu>Connectivity</guisubmenu><guimenuitem> Windows Shares</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This is especially useful if you are a member of a &Windows; <acronym>NT</acronym> domain. There you can also set your workgroup name, but in most cases this is not required. The worker will ask for your username and password if a default is not set."
msgstr "Pode indicar o nome de usuaria e contrasinal predeterminado no &systemsettings; en <guilabel>Rede e conectividade</guilabel> en <menuchoice><guisubmenu>Compartición</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Comparticións de Windows</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Isto é especialmente útil se é membro dun dominio de &Windows; <acronym>NT</acronym>. Alí tamén pode indicar o nome do grupo, pero na maioría dos casos isto non se require. O kioslave preguntaralle o nome de usuaria e o contrasinal se non hai un predeterminado."
